 :catalog/unreachable
 [{:source "https://www.sec.gov.ph/"
   :what "The home register itself -- RA000483, the Companies Register of the Philippine Securities and Exchange Commission, which GLEIF names as both register of record and validation authority."
   :measured "HTTP 403, 5413 bytes, body titled 'Just a moment...' -- a Cloudflare interstitial. Identical result for https://sec.gov.ph/ and for the site's WordPress JSON endpoint."
   :why-not-worked-around "Getting past it means defeating a bot control, which is out of bounds. The consequence is stated plainly rather than papered over: registration number 0000016342 is carried in this catalog on GLEIF's authority alone."}
  {:source "https://efast.sec.gov.ph/"
   :what "SEC eFAST, the Commission's electronic filing and submission tool -- where Philippine annual reports and financial statements are filed."
   :measured "HTTP 200, 10695 bytes, but the body is 'You need to enable JavaScript to run this app.' The company name appears 0 times."
   :why-not-worked-around "Nothing to anchor on without executing the page's scripts, and the document side is behind a login in any case."}
  {:source "https://esparc.sec.gov.ph/application/search"
   :what "eSPARC, the Commission's registration system -- the only SEC host reachable from here that offers a 'search'."
   :measured "HTTP 200. The form asks for an application reference number plus the authorized representative's e-mail, and is labelled 'For Regular Applications Only'."
   :why-not-worked-around "It searches pending applications, not the register of existing companies. It cannot answer whether 0000016342 belongs to this entity, so no row was written against it."}
  {:source "https://www.sec.gov/cgi-bin/browse-edgar?company=SM+Investments&CIK=&action=getcompany"
   :what "The United States SEC's company search -- checked because GLEIF maps two US ADR ISINs (US78455R2058, US78455R1068) to this LEI."
   :measured "HTTP 403 titled 'SEC.gov | Your Request Originates from an Undeclared Automated Tool'. A guessed CIK against data.sec.gov returned 404."
   :why-not-worked-around "The SEC asks automated clients to declare a contact address in the User-Agent; this gate sends a shared UA that carries none, and the tool is byte-identical across sibling repositories so it is not forked here. Spoofing a browser UA would be evading a bot control. Note this is a refusal, not evidence either way: nothing here establishes whether the entity is an EDGAR registrant, and no row claims it is. The ADR ISINs are cited from GLEIF only."}
  {:source "https://data.gov.ph/api/3/action/package_search?q=companies"
   :what "Open Data Philippines -- checked for a published copy of the company register, the route that worked for New York and Singapore in sibling repositories."
   :measured "HTTP 200, 7364 bytes, but the same Angular application shell is returned for the API path as for the site root. There is no CKAN API behind it."
   :why-not-worked-around "There is nothing to query. The Philippines does not publish the SEC company register through this portal in a form this gate can fetch."}
  {:source "https://edge.pse.com.ph/"
   :what "The PSE EDGE portal root, and its financial-report view for this issuer."
   :measured "HTTP 200 but the root is a JavaScript shell with 0 occurrences of the company name. The financial_reports_view page DOES serve real figures (FY ended Dec 31, 2025; total assets 1,811,801 Php millions), and the stockData page serves live share counts and an 'As of' timestamp."
   :why-not-worked-around "Not a refusal -- deliberately not cited. Those values are correct today and will be replaced at the next filing or the next trading day, so a row anchored on them would report DRIFT for a change that is not drift. Only the server-rendered constants on those pages (ISIN, listing date, security id, issuer name) carry rows."}]}
